<p>William “W. A.” Lanterman was born November 24, 1854, on a farm near Blairstown, New Jersey, to {% person "abraham-lanterman" %}Abraham{% endperson %} and {% person "jane-larue-lanterman" %}Jane LaRue Lanterman{% endperson %}. His siblings included brothers {% person "reuben-lanterman" %}Reuben{% endperson %} and {% person "albert-lanterman" %}Albert{% endperson %} and sisters {% person "retta-lanterman" %}Retta{% endperson %}, {% person "georgia-lanterman-shaw" %}Georgia Shaw{% endperson %}, {% person "ida-lanterman" %}Ida{% endperson %}, {% person "emma-lanterman" %}Emma{% endperson %}, and {% person "elizabeth-lanterman-staley" %}Elizabeth Staley{% endperson %}.</p>

<p>Lanterman attended Blair Presbyterial Academy and remained in Blairstown until age 20. In 1875, he joined two brothers in Fisher, Minnesota. He moved to Crookston in 1877, went to Canada to work for the Hudson's Bay Company two years later, and returned to the United States in 1881. He then joined his brother Albert in business in Hillsboro, Dakota Territory.</p>

