  <figure>
    <img src="/assets/images/biographies/william-a-lanterman/409-morton-state-bank-cropped-1915.jpg" alt="State Bank of Morton County around 1915">
  </figure>
</div>

<p>Lanterman helped found the State Bank of Morton County in 1892 and served as its first president. He was also president of Mandan Loan &amp; Investment Company, vice president of First National Bank in New Salem, and president of the North Dakota Bankers Association's Missouri Slope District in 1918.</p>

<p>He led the Mandan Commercial Club, predecessor of the Chamber of Commerce, for many years and served on the Mandan Creamery and Produce Company board. In May 1901, he briefly partnered with {% person "c-f-ellis-sr" %}C. F. Ellis Sr.{% endperson %} in a real-estate, insurance, and loan agency. Ellis bought him out during the winter of 1901–02 and renamed the business the Ellis Agency.</p>

