    <figcaption>Lanterman residence, 303 Third Avenue Northwest</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<p>William, Albert, and Ellis constructed several of Mandan's larger homes. William's principal residence, built in 1901, stood at 303 Third Avenue Northwest. After William and Harriet moved to Glendale, California, in 1921, they subdivided the property and added a smaller house at 301 Third Avenue in 1923.</p>

<p>Lanterman married {% person "harriet-maria-shaw-lanterman" %}Harriet Maria Shaw{% endperson %} in Racine, Wisconsin, on March 22, 1886. They had four children: {% person "betty-bessie-larue-ripley" %}Betty “Bessie” LaRue Ripley{% endperson %}, {% person "eunice-c-ordway" %}Eunice C. Ordway{% endperson %}, {% person "alton-d-lanterman" %}Alton D.{% endperson %}, and {% person "horace-w-lanterman" %}Horace W.{% endperson %} Alton died in 1907 at age 13.</p>

<p>Lanterman was a Master Mason, a Presbyterian, and a Democrat. Harriet died in Los Angeles in March 1924. Early in 1925, William and his son Horace traveled around the world. Soon after returning to Mandan in May, William became ill. He slowly recovered but relapsed after immediately returning to work and died June 19, 1925. His funeral was held at First Presbyterian Church, and he was buried beside Harriet at Forest Lawn Memorial Park in Glendale.</p>
